<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Poland, Lithuania and Russia</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Brzesc Kujawski</h1><p class="st-meta">1267 CE – 1332 CE (approx.) · capital Brzesc Kujawski</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The small Kuyavian duchy of Wladyslaw the Elbow-high, the starting point of the duke who reunited Poland in 1320.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/casimir-i-of-kuyavia">Casimir I of Kuyavia</a> died in 1267, his sons divided the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-kuyavia">Duchy of Kuyavia</a>, and the southern part around Brzesc Kujawski went to the young <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wladyslaw-i-lokietek">Wladyslaw</a> and his brother Casimir. Wladyslaw, nicknamed the Elbow-high for his small stature, was born nearby around 1260.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Brzesc was a modest farming land on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vistula">Vistula</a> plain, bordered by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/state-of-the-teutonic-order">State of the Teutonic Order</a>. From this small base <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wladyslaw-i-lokietek">Wladyslaw I</a> gathered further duchies, including <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-sieradz">Sieradz</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-leczyca">Leczyca</a>, and after long struggles with Bohemian and Silesian rivals he was crowned King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> in 1320.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After 1320 the duchy merged into the reunited <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-poland-1025-1385">Kingdom of Poland</a> (1025-1385). In 1332 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Knights</a> occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuyavia">Kuyavia</a> during their war with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, and it was returned to the Polish Crown by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-kalisz-1343">Treaty of Kalisz</a> in 1343.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-brzesc-kujawski.jpg" alt="Duchy of Brzesc Kujawski" width="320" height="219"><figcaption>Image: HWsnajper · CC BY-SA 3.0 pl · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ratusz_1824_miasto_Brze%C5%9Bc_Kujawski,_gm._Brze%C5%9Bc_Kujawski,_pow._W%C5%82oc%C5%82awski.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1267 CE – 1332 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Brzesc Kujawski</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Wladyslaw I the Elbow-high</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Polish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/poland">Poland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Brzesc Kujawski</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1300&amp;focus=duchy-of-brzesc-kujawski" aria-label="Duchy of Brzesc Kujawski on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5104 364 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Brzesc Kujawski lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5424 620L5409 614M5424 620L5451 561M5424 620L5457 692"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5409 614h0M5451 561h0M5457 692h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5424 620h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5424 620h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1300&amp;focus=duchy-of-brzesc-kujawski">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
